   871                              <1> ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return AL = 0 if it
   872                              <1> ; was ')' and 2 if it was ']'. Brackets of both kinds count together;
   873                              <1> ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for '\' with
   874                              <1> ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
   875                              <1> ; anyway). ECX counts the open levels, from 1 for the one we are in.
   876                              <1> ;
   877                              <1> ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
   878                              <1> ; which is always the one just before where it starts: '(' must end at ')',
   879                              <1> ; '[' at ']', and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
   880                              <1> ; quote counts as running into it. '\' takes either closer. V_SKAT keeps the
